# MCP LSP

The in-tree MCP compatibility transports are declared once by the
client-neutral `tools/node/dev/mcp.manifest.json` and projected into Codex and
Cursor by `tools/node/dev/generate-configs`. Generated absolute-path client
files are machine-local state, not additional manifest authority.

Install the **`idol-dev`** agent skill with `./tools/node/dev/install-skills`.
MCP server and tool names remain bootstrap transport until cutover completes.

Do not add host OS API calls or host-shaped wrappers to canonical source until
`docs/spec/host.md` closure is implemented (`GAP-154`). Host APIs belong at
ingress/egress bootstrap boundaries only.

MCP health requires real JSON-RPC initialize and gate execution, not config
presence or compilation. Protocol stdout must contain protocol data only;
diagnostics belong on stderr.

`duo_agent_session_start` on every MCP server returns `infer_one`, `harness_seams`,
and combined `harness_context`. Agents must run the seam audit before code and query
semantic demand before adding `:to(T)`.
